      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨p,q⟩=2{p}_{1}{q}_{1}+2{p}_{2}{q}_{2}+3{p}_{3}{q}_{3}.$ Find $⟨p,q⟩$, if\n\n$$\np=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p,q⟩ & =2{p}_{1}{q}_{1}+2{p}_{2}{q}_{2}+3{p}_{3}{q}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-12-24 \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
